    "narrative": "The LawDog core is anchored today by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who boasts the day\u2019s highest efficiency score (81.066). His favorable matchup against Singer, bolstered by an elite 40-PA BvP history and a prime #2 spot in the order, makes him our clear standout. **Cal Raleigh** (76.47) and **Daulton Varsho** (72.31) also provide strong production; **Cal Raleigh** benefits significantly from the Lauer matchup, while **Daulton Varsho** is maximizing a massive +10% platoon boost against the right-handed Littell. We are also looking for a rebound performance from **Gleyber Torres** (67.52), whose matchup against Rogers is the ideal environment to leverage his +13% platoon edge and top-of-the-order opportunity.\n\nWhile our starting nine is set, the decision to bench **Gavin Sheets** (45.14) and **Jonathan Aranda** (44.68) was a narrow call. **Gavin Sheets** offered the most resistance, as his strong platoon dynamic against a righty kept his score in the mid-40s, but he ultimately fell behind the higher-floor profiles of **Tyler Freeman** and **Geraldo Perdomo**. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on the risks inherent in today's slate. **Taylor Ward** (53.36) faces the toughest test of the day against the formidable Skubal; despite a helpful platoon edge, his raw projection is suppressed by the elite opponent. Furthermore, while **Luis Arraez** (61.40) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (54.45) receive a wind-aided boost, they are battling a significantly tilted matchup against Pannone, leaving them sensitive to early-game volatility. Proceed with confidence in the top tier, but monitor the game caps closely as the evening progresses.",
